  "result": "All done. The full suite passes (6 tests) and the edge cases behave sensibly.\n\n**Changes, all in `catalog/service.py`:**\n\n- **`find(substring)`** returns copies of records whose title contains the substring, compared with `casefold` so matching is case-insensitive, in creation order.\n- **`export()`** returns `json.dumps` of the record list, so the array is in creation order and each record keeps its id.\n- **`import_(dump)`** parses the dump, validates it is a JSON array of `{id, title, author}` records with string ids, and inserts them with their original ids. It raises `ValueError` on malformed input, on duplicate ids within the dump, or on an id that already exists in the catalog, and loads nothing in those cases. Because the project uses sequential integer ids, it also advances the counter past any numeric imported id so later `create` calls never reuse an imported id.\n\nNothing under `tests/` was touched.",
